id:              SRG-APP-000142-WSR-000089
group:           V-206386
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000382
control_rev5:    CM-7

contribution:    Splunk can be bound to one address and one port on each of its listeners:
                 Splunk Web through its socket host and port, and the daemon's own
                 listeners through the bind address in the launch configuration.

governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] server.socket_host not_in 0.0.0.0|::
check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_BINDIP non_empty
check:           web.conf [settings] mgmtHostPort present
check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_BINDIP not_in 0.0.0.0|::|*
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_BINDIP https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] httpport https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] mgmtHostPort https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] server.socket_host https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.6/start-splunk-enterprise-and-perform-initial-tasks/bind-splunk-to-an-ip
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] httpport present
                 reason: "httpport = <positive integer>. The TCP port on which Splunk Web
                         listens for incoming connections. Must be present for Splunk Web to
                         start. If omitted or 0 the server will NOT start an http listener.
                         If using SSL, set to the HTTPS port number. Default: 8000"
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Which address the instance is permitted to use, and any further
                 restriction on who can reach it, carried by the host's network
                 configuration and the firewall.
external:        Confirming from a client that no other address answers, which the check
                 performs by test rather than by reading configuration.

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000142-WSR-000089 check and fix text;
                 web.conf.spec:28 (httpport, default 8000), web.conf.spec:844
                 (server.socket_host, 0.0.0.0 means any active interface), web.conf.spec:35
                 (mgmtHostPort), splunk-launch.conf.spec:79 (SPLUNK_BINDIP)
finding:         Splunk Web or the daemon is left listening on every interface of the host,
                 or its port is not declared, so the application does not confine itself to
                 one specified address and port.
